# A name a body binds by its own code is the body's own, whatever expression binds it (#318): `_loud` makes `loud` from
# the samples it is handed, by an expression no step makes (`samples.abs() > 0`), and hands back a mask made of it.
# `loud` is no module's name and no value from beyond: closed, `_loud` takes only the samples its call hands it. Its
# contrast, `_at_floor`, reads the module's `FLOOR`, which no code of the route makes: a value from beyond, by its name,
# since the step takes two tensors.

route marks.peaks
step peaks/_loud

line entry > peaks call
line Tensor·samples > peaks value                           # `print(samples * mask)`
line Tensor·samples > peaks/_loud value
line peaks/_loud > Tensor·mask@peaks/_loud value
line Tensor·mask@peaks/_loud > peaks value
line peaks > Screen own

home Tensor·samples peaks
home Tensor·mask@peaks/_loud peaks

side entry left
side Screen right

route marks.floor
step floor/_at_floor

line entry > floor call
line Tensor·samples > floor value
line Tensor·samples > floor/_at_floor value
line Tensor·FLOOR > floor/_at_floor value                    # the module's floor, from beyond
line floor/_at_floor > Tensor·mask@floor/_at_floor value
line Tensor·mask@floor/_at_floor > floor value
line floor > Screen own

home Tensor·samples floor
home Tensor·FLOOR floor
home Tensor·mask@floor/_at_floor floor

side entry left
side Screen right
